Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:10:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] leds: flash: qcom: Fix the safety timer by one step
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The safety timer runs for one 10 ms step more than the value in its
register: the largest timeout the driver offers, 1280 ms, only fits the
7-bit field as 127. The vendor drivers for these PMICs program
(timeout / 10) - 1 accordingly, while this one programs timeout / 10,
so every flash lasts 10 ms longer than asked. Subtract the extra step.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c b/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c
index b03a6833e..e5820091d 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c
@@ -397,7 +397,10 @@ static int set_flash_timeout(struct qcom_flash_led *led, u32 timeout_ms)
 	for (i = 0; i < led->chan_count; i++) {
 		chan_id = led->chan_id[i];
 
+		/* The timer runs for one step more than its value */
 		timer = timeout_ms / FLASH_TIMER_STEP_MS;
+		if (timer)
+			timer--;
 		timer = clamp_t(u8, timer, 0, FLASH_TIMER_VAL_MASK);
 
 		if (timeout_ms)
